(1215727, 153299, 18191, '<td valign="top">My biggest concern in this image is the grain. It is not that I am against grain... I actualyl usually prefer it... but for Ansel Adams.. he usuall used ISO6 or ISO25 film... and grain was very rarely seen. I will vote aside from that though...just a thought.</td>', 'My biggest concern in this image is the grain. It is not that I am against grain... I actualyl usually prefer it... but for Ansel Adams.. he usuall used ISO6 or ISO25 film... and grain was very rarely seen. I will vote aside from that though...just a thought.', '2005-03-08 20:20:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1215731, 152852, 16230, '<td valign="top">I love everything about this photo... except for the sky. The green and gray jagginess doesn''t fit the rest of the image IMHO. A very nice photo otherwise.</td>', 'I love everything about this photo... except for the sky. The green and gray jagginess doesn''t fit the rest of the image IMHO. A very nice photo otherwise.', '2005-03-08 20:21:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1215737, 153030, 16230, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice image with a good range of tones. Would be even better without the blown highlights in the clouds, and a smaller (or no) border. Good work!</td>', 'This is a very nice image with a good range of tones. Would be even better without the blown highlights in the clouds, and a smaller (or no) border. Good work!', '2005-03-08 20:25:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1215743, 152486, 16230, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice image. A nicely dramatic composition with a good range of tones. I love the way the white cliffs stand out boldly and lead the eye into the image. It gives the image a nice feeling of depth. The image appears to be somewhat over-sharpened though. You might have been better off without the border, and with the image itself a bit larger. I''d love to see a high-res version of this photo. Very nice work!</td>', 'This is a very nice image. A nicely dramatic composition with a good range of tones. I love the way the white cliffs stand out boldly and lead the eye into the image. It gives the image a nice feeling of depth. The image appears to be somewhat over-sharpened though. You might have been better off without the border, and with the image itself a bit larger. I''d love to see a high-res version of this photo. Very nice work!', '2005-03-08 20:37:22.000000', NULL, 1),
