(1221217, 151561, 30018, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image.  Looks like this should be on the October page of the calendar.  &lt;8&gt;<br/></td>', 'Beautiful image.  Looks like this should be on the October page of the calendar.  <8>', '2005-03-11 05:22:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221219, 153288, 30018, '<td valign="top">Beautiful capture.  This should be on the December page of the Calendar &lt;8&gt;</td>', 'Beautiful capture.  This should be on the December page of the Calendar <8>', '2005-03-11 05:26:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221221, 152958, 30018, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is great.  This one belongs on the August page of the calendar &lt;8&gt;</td>', 'Wow, this is great.  This one belongs on the August page of the calendar <8>', '2005-03-11 05:28:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221224, 153088, 30018, '<td valign="top">Great photography, as you captured the tonal range, and Ansel would have been proud of you for that.  I''m not sure if this is the type of subject or composition he would have chosen.  The dust spots in the black background bother me a lot.  But the textures and tones in the leaves themselves are wonderful. &lt;7&gt;</td>', 'Great photography, as you captured the tonal range, and Ansel would have been proud of you for that.  I''m not sure if this is the type of subject or composition he would have chosen.  The dust spots in the black background bother me a lot.  But the textures and tones in the leaves themselves are wonderful. <7>', '2005-03-11 05:31:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221225, 153392, 30018, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  Amazing what nature can do.  Oh, and your photograph is very nice as well &lt;LOL&gt;  This seems just a little flat, but not bad.  &lt;7&gt;</td>', 'Beautiful.  Amazing what nature can do.  Oh, and your photograph is very nice as well <LOL>  This seems just a little flat, but not bad.  <7>', '2005-03-11 05:33:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221227, 153117, 30018, '<td valign="top">Outstanding.  The February page of the calendar. &lt;8&gt;</td>', 'Outstanding.  The February page of the calendar. <8>', '2005-03-11 05:35:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221230, 153030, 30018, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image.  Let''s put this on the March page of the calendar as it looks as if the Ides of March are hard a work here.  &lt;8&gt;</td>', 'Beautiful image.  Let''s put this on the March page of the calendar as it looks as if the Ides of March are hard a work here.  <8>', '2005-03-11 05:38:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221232, 153026, 30018, '<td valign="top">I would like to include this one in the calendar placing it on the July page &lt;8&gt;</td>', 'I would like to include this one in the calendar placing it on the July page <8>', '2005-03-11 05:39:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221238, 153005, 6999, '<td valign="top">The over-exposure of the clouds is my major problem with this: all that remains here is the shapes, with no sense of the different tones that should be there. Obviously Idon''t know what type of camera you''re using, but I would have metered fro the clouds to find my exposure setting here (then you would know the brightest part of the image), or if necessary the very edges of the rock, so that you still get that brightness in the metered area, and hoped that the range of the camera would cope with the comparative darkness of the rocks, and could be brought back in editing. Compoaitionally, I think this is too complex to be Adams-like: most of his images are of very strong shapes, without a lot of confusion of different shapes that you have here. The surface weathering on those rocks is beautifully caught, however, giving them some sense of real ''life'', which i like.</td>', 'The over-exposure of the clouds is my major problem with this: all that remains here is the shapes, with no sense of the different tones that should be there. Obviously Idon''t know what type of camera you''re using, but I would have metered fro the clouds to find my exposure setting here (then you would know the brightest part of the image), or if necessary the very edges of the rock, so that you still get that brightness in the metered area, and hoped that the range of the camera would cope with the comparative darkness of the rocks, and could be brought back in editing. Compoaitionally, I think this is too complex to be Adams-like: most of his images are of very strong shapes, without a lot of confusion of different shapes that you have here. The surface weathering on those rocks is beautifully caught, however, giving them some sense of real ''life'', which i like.', '2005-03-11 05:46:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221243, 153362, 6999, '<td valign="top">Works for me as an AA type of subject, though i think he would have found more contrast within the tree in a print than there is here. I also find tthe composition a touch congested for AA - all elements seem crowded into the left-hand side of frame. I can see the effectiveness (photographically and challenge-wise) of the distance available image right, and that shooting from any further left would have ruined the light, but nevertheless that crowding is a bit of a problem to my eye. I like your care with overall range though, very effective.</td>', 'Works for me as an AA type of subject, though i think he would have found more contrast within the tree in a print than there is here. I also find tthe composition a touch congested for AA - all elements seem crowded into the left-hand side of frame. I can see the effectiveness (photographically and challenge-wise) of the distance available image right, and that shooting from any further left would have ruined the light, but nevertheless that crowding is a bit of a problem to my eye. I like your care with overall range though, very effective.', '2005-03-11 05:51:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221245, 153388, 6999, '<td valign="top">Almost believeable, certainly. A couple of drawbacks for me: lack of foreground or even middle-distance interest, something to give a retreating dynamic into the frame, and a lack of life in the sky - where i think this cries out for a careful selection and pushing of contrast: it''s that regular grey of those clouds, i think, where one would hope for more variety of tone. Absolutely the expected subject, and well worked tonally - the mountain itself really has that AA feel.</td>', 'Almost believeable, certainly. A couple of drawbacks for me: lack of foreground or even middle-distance interest, something to give a retreating dynamic into the frame, and a lack of life in the sky - where i think this cries out for a careful selection and pushing of contrast: it''s that regular grey of those clouds, i think, where one would hope for more variety of tone. Absolutely the expected subject, and well worked tonally - the mountain itself really has that AA feel.', '2005-03-11 05:54:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221250, 152213, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure. There are very very strong elements here - tonal range, very zone system - but other elements seem out of place. What looks like fill-flash, which could simply be reflection from ground, feels out of place to me for AA''s work, and a certain confusion from the vegetation likewise seems to be something he''d have avoided. Composition is strong, though perhaps not really an AA type of thing, and the perspective distortion is perhaps out of place too. All of which sounds highly critical, so i should add that I do really like this image, and think it works well for the challenge ... I''m just a hyper-critical kind of commenter :-)</td>', 'I''m not sure. There are very very strong elements here - tonal range, very zone system - but other elements seem out of place. What looks like fill-flash, which could simply be reflection from ground, feels out of place to me for AA''s work, and a certain confusion from the vegetation likewise seems to be something he''d have avoided. Composition is strong, though perhaps not really an AA type of thing, and the perspective distortion is perhaps out of place too. All of which sounds highly critical, so i should add that I do really like this image, and think it works well for the challenge ... I''m just a hyper-critical kind of commenter :-)', '2005-03-11 05:59:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221252, 152756, 6999, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image, but the treatment is just not Adams-like. What really seems out of place is the lack of contrast in the land areas - the range there is quite restricted, and i would have selected it and pushed the contrast quite a bit. Also the over-exposure of the sky areas is just too much to my eye (some would be acceptable, to give that sense of brightness, but i just can''t see this range as being typicla of AA.</td>', 'Wonderful image, but the treatment is just not Adams-like. What really seems out of place is the lack of contrast in the land areas - the range there is quite restricted, and i would have selected it and pushed the contrast quite a bit. Also the over-exposure of the sky areas is just too much to my eye (some would be acceptable, to give that sense of brightness, but i just can''t see this range as being typicla of AA.', '2005-03-11 06:03:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221278, 153367, 2798, '<td valign="top">There is a very odd liquid look to this image. Im not sure what you''ve done but it looks like a really extreme neatimage effect. There are patches of blur and patches of sharpness. Strange and surreal but not really to my taste. Good contrast and choice of subject. 6</td>', 'There is a very odd liquid look to this image. Im not sure what you''ve done but it looks like a really extreme neatimage effect. There are patches of blur and patches of sharpness. Strange and surreal but not really to my taste. Good contrast and choice of subject. 6', '2005-03-11 06:49:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221280, 153309, 2798, '<td valign="top">Lovely scene that feels a touch over sharpened. 8</td>', 'Lovely scene that feels a touch over sharpened. 8', '2005-03-11 06:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221281, 153286, 2798, '<td valign="top">Just a little more sharpening perhaps to bring up the detail there. Nice idea. 6</td>', 'Just a little more sharpening perhaps to bring up the detail there. Nice idea. 6', '2005-03-11 06:54:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221283, 152610, 2798, '<td valign="top">Some really obvious dodging and burning adds drama to an otherwise undramatic scene. Feels oddly surreal and conflicted as a result. 6</td>', 'Some really obvious dodging and burning adds drama to an otherwise undramatic scene. Feels oddly surreal and conflicted as a result. 6', '2005-03-11 06:55:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221284, 152486, 27137, '<td valign="top">very nice</td>', 'very nice', '2005-03-11 06:56:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221287, 153381, 2798, '<td valign="top">There''s nothing in this picture to really look at. It''s a jumble of ill focused twigs and branches that gives the eye nowhere to start. I would have preferred if you''d found some detail in the branches to focus on. Something interesting to the eye that gave me a starting point for the image. 5</td>', 'There''s nothing in this picture to really look at. It''s a jumble of ill focused twigs and branches that gives the eye nowhere to start. I would have preferred if you''d found some detail in the branches to focus on. Something interesting to the eye that gave me a starting point for the image. 5', '2005-03-11 06:59:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221288, 153287, 27137, '<td valign="top">THe railing directs me to the the church in the right side,  nice, how ever the trees are a bit distracting</td>', 'THe railing directs me to the the church in the right side,  nice, how ever the trees are a bit distracting', '2005-03-11 07:00:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221291, 153292, 2798, '<td valign="top">A lovely scene but too dark and not sharp enough. A real pity too because with just a little more work this would be a winner. 5</td>', 'A lovely scene but too dark and not sharp enough. A real pity too because with just a little more work this would be a winner. 5', '2005-03-11 07:01:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221326, 153117, 6999, '<td valign="top">This is a bit too christmas-cardy for AA, I would say. His images, to my mind, are not usually so twee. The tonality is fine, as one would hope given the massive range that departing from black and white allows you.</td>', 'This is a bit too christmas-cardy for AA, I would say. His images, to my mind, are not usually so twee. The tonality is fine, as one would hope given the massive range that departing from black and white allows you.', '2005-03-11 08:08:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221338, 153147, 19959, '<td valign="top">nice. Interesting sky and composition.</td>', 'nice. Interesting sky and composition.', '2005-03-11 08:21:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221347, 153329, 11693, '<td valign="top">When I first saw your shot I knew it was a 10 to me.  It has the tonal range and razor sharpness that is Ansel.  It is hard to get the razor edge without a field camera, but you seemed to have done it.  This is realy on par with the master.  Great shot!!!!!</td>', 'When I first saw your shot I knew it was a 10 to me.  It has the tonal range and razor sharpness that is Ansel.  It is hard to get the razor edge without a field camera, but you seemed to have done it.  This is realy on par with the master.  Great shot!!!!!', '2005-03-11 08:33:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221350, 152894, 11693, '<td valign="top">I like the shot, but I do not like the brown tint. 6</td>', 'I like the shot, but I do not like the brown tint. 6', '2005-03-11 08:37:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221351, 152852, 27767, '<td valign="top">Composition: 9, Love the framing of the first door<br/>Technical: 8, Great tone range.  Only thing I can suggest is to decrease the jpeg compression slightly so the shades in the sky are a little smoother<br/>Appeal: 9<br/>Challenge: 10, Shot could be directly out of Ansel''s camera if I didn''t know better<br/>Overall Calculated Average Score: 9</td>', 'Composition: 9, Love the framing of the first doorTechnical: 8, Great tone range.  Only thing I can suggest is to decrease the jpeg compression slightly so the shades in the sky are a little smootherAppeal: 9Challenge: 10, Shot could be directly out of Ansel''s camera if I didn''t know betterOverall Calculated Average Score: 9', '2005-03-11 08:37:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221352, 152330, 11693, '<td valign="top">Good shot, BUT this really has to be a B&amp;W photo to be considered Ansel to me. 3</td>', 'Good shot, BUT this really has to be a B&W photo to be considered Ansel to me. 3', '2005-03-11 08:39:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221361, 152330, 15690, '<td valign="top">A pleasure to see some color after all the black and whites.  Good luck</td>', 'A pleasure to see some color after all the black and whites.  Good luck', '2005-03-11 08:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221375, 153274, 16739, '<td valign="top">is that grat neck  , ny</td>', 'is that grat neck  , ny', '2005-03-11 09:06:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221386, 153288, 14986, '<td valign="top">I really like the tones in this shot, and the reflection is great.  It''s a good, clear shot, but something about the composition and subject is lacking for me.  I''m not sure what it is.  There''s a lot going on in the photo, and the b/w probably makes it appear busier than it really is because of the similar tones throughout.  In color, my eye would have some natural "sections" of the photo on which to focus.  It looks like a pretty spot, but I''m not sure if I think it''s the best location for b/w.    I still scored this pretty high because I thought you did do a good job with the b/w tones, and for the clarity of the shot.   Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'I really like the tones in this shot, and the reflection is great.  It''s a good, clear shot, but something about the composition and subject is lacking for me.  I''m not sure what it is.  There''s a lot going on in the photo, and the b/w probably makes it appear busier than it really is because of the similar tones throughout.  In color, my eye would have some natural "sections" of the photo on which to focus.  It looks like a pretty spot, but I''m not sure if I think it''s the best location for b/w.    I still scored this pretty high because I thought you did do a good job with the b/w tones, and for the clarity of the shot.   Hope this is helpful.', '2005-03-11 09:15:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221391, 152341, 14986, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely b/w shot.   The focus, to me, seems just a bit on the softer side and I think I would prefer it to be sharper.   I probably would have played around a bit more with the composition, but I like this as well.   It looks to me like you''ve lost a bit of the detail in the upper petals, and the flower doesn''t really "jump" out at me as the viewer.   All that being said, I still like the shot very much.  Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'This is a lovely b/w shot.   The focus, to me, seems just a bit on the softer side and I think I would prefer it to be sharper.   I probably would have played around a bit more with the composition, but I like this as well.   It looks to me like you''ve lost a bit of the detail in the upper petals, and the flower doesn''t really "jump" out at me as the viewer.   All that being said, I still like the shot very much.  Hope this is helpful.', '2005-03-11 09:18:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221393, 153218, 14986, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition and idea on this shot.  I would have scored it a point higher if there had been a little more detail in the darker leaves.   I think you did a good job on the background with this and overall I like it alot.</td>', 'I really like the composition and idea on this shot.  I would have scored it a point higher if there had been a little more detail in the darker leaves.   I think you did a good job on the background with this and overall I like it alot.', '2005-03-11 09:20:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221395, 152214, 14986, '<td valign="top">This is a pretty clear shot of your subject.   I think, for me, it''s lacking in tone a bit.  There doesn''t appear to me to be much variation in the b/w scale compared to some of the other shots.   Also, I think the subject and composition are hurt by all the branches and other wood in the foreground and in back of the subject.    I hope this is helpful.</td>', 'This is a pretty clear shot of your subject.   I think, for me, it''s lacking in tone a bit.  There doesn''t appear to me to be much variation in the b/w scale compared to some of the other shots.   Also, I think the subject and composition are hurt by all the branches and other wood in the foreground and in back of the subject.    I hope this is helpful.', '2005-03-11 09:23:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221400, 153303, 14986, '<td valign="top">Cool place for your shot.   I don''t know why, but  I feel like it needs a bit of a counter-clockwise rotation.   Tones aren''t too bad, but I would have liked to have seen a bit more detail and texture to the shot.   The rocks and stones have a rather "flat" appearance to me as far as lighting and b/w tone.    I think this would be a great place to do in color.    Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'Cool place for your shot.   I don''t know why, but  I feel like it needs a bit of a counter-clockwise rotation.   Tones aren''t too bad, but I would have liked to have seen a bit more detail and texture to the shot.   The rocks and stones have a rather "flat" appearance to me as far as lighting and b/w tone.    I think this would be a great place to do in color.    Hope this is helpful.', '2005-03-11 09:27:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221406, 153181, 14986, '<td valign="top">Neat idea for the challenge.   The focus seems good here, but something about the shot is preventing it from really "popping" out at me.   There appears to be a lot of texture here, but I don''t get a really strong feeling of it from the photo.   Maybe a closer shot or different lighting?  The b/w tones seem a bit warm, and maybe the texture would show better in a harsher b/w?   I also would have liked it better with the top portion cropped more...just about to a square.  I did that on my monitor and I liked it that way.  I''m no expert, but  I did give this an above average score.   I like the idea a lot.  I hope this is helpful.</td>', 'Neat idea for the challenge.   The focus seems good here, but something about the shot is preventing it from really "popping" out at me.   There appears to be a lot of texture here, but I don''t get a really strong feeling of it from the photo.   Maybe a closer shot or different lighting?  The b/w tones seem a bit warm, and maybe the texture would show better in a harsher b/w?   I also would have liked it better with the top portion cropped more...just about to a square.  I did that on my monitor and I liked it that way.  I''m no expert, but  I did give this an above average score.   I like the idea a lot.  I hope this is helpful.', '2005-03-11 09:33:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221435, 153255, 26756, '<td valign="top">One of the most attractive flower pics I''ve seen in quite some time.  Nicely posed and the surroundings are very complimentary to the flower.  Nice tones.</td>', 'One of the most attractive flower pics I''ve seen in quite some time.  Nicely posed and the surroundings are very complimentary to the flower.  Nice tones.', '2005-03-11 10:08:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221460, 152702, 29797, '<td valign="top">I really like this one. Good choice in waiting for the light to hit the rock face and leaving the hillside dark.  Nice framing trees in the foreground.</td>', 'I really like this one. Good choice in waiting for the light to hit the rock face and leaving the hillside dark.  Nice framing trees in the foreground.', '2005-03-11 10:28:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221464, 153182, 29797, '<td valign="top">3rd or 4th time viewing this photo, everything else is so captivating, I just now noticed the stairs/pathway. Nice capture.</td>', '3rd or 4th time viewing this photo, everything else is so captivating, I just now noticed the stairs/pathway. Nice capture.', '2005-03-11 10:31:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221486, 152852, 4285, '<td valign="top">I love the image. Too bad that there''s lots of artifacts and vertical banding in you sky  (very strange effect from a camera - I''ve seen scanners do this - please don''t take this as an accusation, it''s not). Again very lovely image.</td>', 'I love the image. Too bad that there''s lots of artifacts and vertical banding in you sky  (very strange effect from a camera - I''ve seen scanners do this - please don''t take this as an accusation, it''s not). Again very lovely image.', '2005-03-11 10:54:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221577, 152736, 5728, '<td valign="top">I only know one person in Naples, Chiq! Good one!</td>', 'I only know one person in Naples, Chiq! Good one!', '2005-03-11 12:25:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221620, 153333, 32236, '<td valign="top">Dreamy. I like this one because it has a point of interest. Think I would like it more with some of the lower beach cropped out and a lower horizon. Nice.</td>', 'Dreamy. I like this one because it has a point of interest. Think I would like it more with some of the lower beach cropped out and a lower horizon. Nice.', '2005-03-11 12:58:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221627, 152214, 8860, '<td valign="top">Love the tree and the scene. Shot is very over-sharpened though. Tones are quite rich but a little too harsh for true AA. The sharpening coupled with the many branches visible makes this very busy to look at. OK composition but the tree cropped at the top is a shame and eye-level POV is quite bland.<br/> <br/>To improve this I would have got closer and looked upwards from a low vantage point. This would show more detail, add some drama and, if you were to expose right, get a long DOF which is very typical of AA.</td>', 'Love the tree and the scene. Shot is very over-sharpened though. Tones are quite rich but a little too harsh for true AA. The sharpening coupled with the many branches visible makes this very busy to look at. OK composition but the tree cropped at the top is a shame and eye-level POV is quite bland. To improve this I would have got closer and looked upwards from a low vantage point. This would show more detail, add some drama and, if you were to expose right, get a long DOF which is very typical of AA.', '2005-03-11 13:03:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221635, 153231, 8860, '<td valign="top">While I know he took portraits, this strikes as too flippant in its execution to echo the great man''s technique and choice of subject. OUtside of the challenge it''s a good portrait, but for me, since the focus is Ansel Adams, it''s a bit weak. The tones are very harsh too (narrow range) leaving the blacks too black and the whites too bright. Your editing is a little conspicuous on the hair also. Good, offset composition.</td>', 'While I know he took portraits, this strikes as too flippant in its execution to echo the great man''s technique and choice of subject. OUtside of the challenge it''s a good portrait, but for me, since the focus is Ansel Adams, it''s a bit weak. The tones are very harsh too (narrow range) leaving the blacks too black and the whites too bright. Your editing is a little conspicuous on the hair also. Good, offset composition.', '2005-03-11 13:06:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221638, 151432, 8860, '<td valign="top">Definitely a more unusual approach. I like it, although the tones for me are a little too narrow in range with some hot spots in the whites.</td>', 'Definitely a more unusual approach. I like it, although the tones for me are a little too narrow in range with some hot spots in the whites.', '2005-03-11 13:08:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221654, 153296, 8860, '<td valign="top">Nice subject and composition. Editing a bit crude with some prominent haloing round tree. AA factor not particularly strong.</td>', 'Nice subject and composition. Editing a bit crude with some prominent haloing round tree. AA factor not particularly strong.', '2005-03-11 13:13:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221659, 152770, 8860, '<td valign="top">Lovely scene with some decent foreground interest. Light is strong and effective. Foreground mass is too dark and - I don''t often say this(!) - the sky could have been burned some more to add some depth and balance. AA factor is quite strong but it lacks some tonal range to truly reflect his style.</td>', 'Lovely scene with some decent foreground interest. Light is strong and effective. Foreground mass is too dark and - I don''t often say this(!) - the sky could have been burned some more to add some depth and balance. AA factor is quite strong but it lacks some tonal range to truly reflect his style.', '2005-03-11 13:16:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221666, 153392, 8860, '<td valign="top">A lovely subject spoiled only by too much prominent editing. Tonal range is not broad enough (too much mid grey) for an AA, but the subject would have been convincing if you hadn''t lost the top, which is a real breaker for this image. I love gnarly would like this and I''d love to see it re-shot without the special FX and a more dynamic range.</td>', 'A lovely subject spoiled only by too much prominent editing. Tonal range is not broad enough (too much mid grey) for an AA, but the subject would have been convincing if you hadn''t lost the top, which is a real breaker for this image. I love gnarly would like this and I''d love to see it re-shot without the special FX and a more dynamic range.', '2005-03-11 13:19:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221671, 152770, 16636, '<td valign="top">This is great, wish the sky could have been burnt in a little more to emphasise the mood. Hope this does well for you</td>', 'This is great, wish the sky could have been burnt in a little more to emphasise the mood. Hope this does well for you', '2005-03-11 13:21:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221675, 153150, 8860, '<td valign="top">Well that makes two of you! I have to say that I do prefer the other shot of this lovely place. Tones are not broad enough for AA and that mass at the front really needed some light on it as it''s gone black - not an approach AA would have taken.</td>', 'Well that makes two of you! I have to say that I do prefer the other shot of this lovely place. Tones are not broad enough for AA and that mass at the front really needed some light on it as it''s gone black - not an approach AA would have taken.', '2005-03-11 13:22:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1221677, 153342, 16636, '<td valign="top">unfortunately it needs more in the sky which would have tuned this into a stunning image</td>', 'unfortunately it needs more in the sky which would have tuned this into a stunning image', '2005-03-11 13:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
