(1223315, 153138, 28141, '<td valign="top">Seems kinda purple.  Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.</td>', 'Seems kinda purple.  Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.', '2005-03-12 14:47:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1223316, 153231, 28141, '<td valign="top">Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.</td>', 'Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.', '2005-03-12 14:48:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1223317, 153257, 28141, '<td valign="top">Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.</td>', 'Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.', '2005-03-12 14:48:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1223318, 153117, 28141, '<td valign="top">It''s hard to tell, but this looks like it''s in color.  Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.</td>', 'It''s hard to tell, but this looks like it''s in color.  Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.', '2005-03-12 14:49:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1223321, 152363, 28141, '<td valign="top">Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.</td>', 'Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.', '2005-03-12 14:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1223322, 153026, 28141, '<td valign="top">Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.  I do like this shot though.</td>', 'Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.  I do like this shot though.', '2005-03-12 14:52:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1223326, 152330, 28141, '<td valign="top">Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.</td>', 'Yes, he did take some portraits and color shots, but in my opinion they are not what define his style.  Everyone experiments, but one''s style is what is common and familiar.  If every type of photo someone ever took were included in a description of their style, then every photographer would have essentially the same style.  In my opion, what defines Ansel Adams'' STYLE is high contrast outdoor black and whites, not every photo he ever took.', '2005-03-12 14:53:09.000000', NULL, 1),
