(1225690, 153246, 23318, '<td valign="top">to those of you that commented, you''re all right. There''s something wrong with the way I''m reducing and editing images, either in the workflow and/or the software. I''m looking into learning a better workflow. <br/> <br/><a href="//www.eckoe.net/dpc/CRW_0757-shouldabeen.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Fullsize better crop</a> <br/> <br/>Above link goes to the crop and detail that I wanted to see in the image, hopefully this would have scored better than the brown. It''s twice the pixels, and the only thing that''s been done with it is a slight curves, and convert to greyscale, then 1:1 cropped to 1280x1280.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-14 02:23:25.</i></td>', 'to those of you that commented, you''re all right. There''s something wrong with the way I''m reducing and editing images, either in the workflow and/or the software. I''m looking into learning a better workflow.  Fullsize better crop  Above link goes to the crop and detail that I wanted to see in the image, hopefully this would have scored better than the brown. It''s twice the pixels, and the only thing that''s been done with it is a slight curves, and convert to greyscale, then 1:1 cropped to 1280x1280.', '2005-03-14 01:41:38.000000', '2005-03-14 02:23:25.000000', 0),
(1225692, 153219, 9668, '<td valign="top">Awsome reading! The question with DPC, though, is to fit outside the box, but inside the challenge, and that is the point reach. Keep it up =)</td>', 'Awsome reading! The question with DPC, though, is to fit outside the box, but inside the challenge, and that is the point reach. Keep it up =)', '2005-03-14 01:43:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225701, 153481, 93, '<td valign="top">Not really an Ansel type photograph.. but I had a sudden urge to submit *SOME*thing at the deadline, and this is what I chose.<br/> <br/>Also, as I said, I had a horrible monitor to process it on.. lol<br/> <br/>To tell you the truth.. a 5.297 surprises the hell out of me. Someone even gave me a 10! lol</td>', 'Not really an Ansel type photograph.. but I had a sudden urge to submit *SOME*thing at the deadline, and this is what I chose. Also, as I said, I had a horrible monitor to process it on.. lol To tell you the truth.. a 5.297 surprises the hell out of me. Someone even gave me a 10! lol', '2005-03-14 01:46:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225705, 152044, 30364, '<td valign="top">I''ve been away Robert, so I''m seeing this challenge for the first time right now.  This is great; it does everything you &amp; Ed Clarke suggested in a forum would be required to do well.  Full tonal range, with retained detail at every point on that range, etc, etc.  Plus it''s a damn fine photograph even without its AA tribute qualities.  Congratulations on this &amp; on your exceptional contribution to the DPC community.</td>', 'I''ve been away Robert, so I''m seeing this challenge for the first time right now.  This is great; it does everything you & Ed Clarke suggested in a forum would be required to do well.  Full tonal range, with retained detail at every point on that range, etc, etc.  Plus it''s a damn fine photograph even without its AA tribute qualities.  Congratulations on this & on your exceptional contribution to the DPC community.', '2005-03-14 01:47:36.000000', NULL, 0),
