(1225866, 152044, 30222, '<td valign="top">perfect composition <br/>i like the agressive tonal touch in contrast to the peaceful scenery<br/>extremely deserved top-10 finish<br/>congratulations Robert</td>', 'perfect composition i like the agressive tonal touch in contrast to the peaceful sceneryextremely deserved top-10 finishcongratulations Robert', '2005-03-14 03:40:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225900, 152754, 29827, '<td valign="top">Thankyou to all who voted - very pleased with my score.<br/> <br/>Jamie</td>', 'Thankyou to all who voted - very pleased with my score. Jamie', '2005-03-14 04:23:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225907, 153148, 2798, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the kind comments. This wasn''t shot specially for the challenge - I happened to be at a family get together that weekend and decided to take an afternoon shooting the seaside. This was my favourite of the day.<br/> <br/>I have since re-done the B&amp;W conversion on this image and controlled the highlights and lowlights in the sky much better. I''ll use the better version for prints.</td>', 'Thanks for all the kind comments. This wasn''t shot specially for the challenge - I happened to be at a family get together that weekend and decided to take an afternoon shooting the seaside. This was my favourite of the day. I have since re-done the B&W conversion on this image and controlled the highlights and lowlights in the sky much better. I''ll use the better version for prints.', '2005-03-14 04:32:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225910, 151701, 33560, '<td valign="top">This was my first photo to clear the 6.0 hurdle.  Thanks to all who left comments.</td>', 'This was my first photo to clear the 6.0 hurdle.  Thanks to all who left comments.', '2005-03-14 04:34:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225912, 152898, 2798, '<td valign="top">I scored this as an 8. It''s well taken and the B&amp;W conversion is good. If there is a problem it''s that there isn''t an identifiable subject for the eye to rest on. My eye hunts around the image but never really stops anywhere. Your scene is well framed, though and at no point is my eye led out of the image.</td>', 'I scored this as an 8. It''s well taken and the B&W conversion is good. If there is a problem it''s that there isn''t an identifiable subject for the eye to rest on. My eye hunts around the image but never really stops anywhere. Your scene is well framed, though and at no point is my eye led out of the image.', '2005-03-14 04:38:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225918, 153333, 8522, '<td valign="top">Well done on your ribbon and fantastic photo... I knew it was just a question of time!</td>', 'Well done on your ribbon and fantastic photo... I knew it was just a question of time!', '2005-03-14 04:42:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225942, 152603, 14656, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the feedback, everyone. The dark line where the mountains meet the sky was the effect of the feathered edge of the brush hitting the mountains while burning the sky. Perhaps I should''ve backed off a bit or dodged them back to a middle tone. I suppose it put many people off.<br/> <br/>I also was tempted to boost the contrast on this image but most of the Ansel photos I studied were similar to this, having a majority of middle tones, a few highlights, and most of the gradation of tones in the sky or clouds.<br/> <br/>I spent about 4 or 5 hours dodging and burning, making sure I kept detail in almost all of the shadowed areas. I made an 8x12 print of this image and it looks amazing! 100x''s better than this websized version. It also appears to have more tonal range and contrast compared to the monitor as well.</td>', 'Thanks for the feedback, everyone. The dark line where the mountains meet the sky was the effect of the feathered edge of the brush hitting the mountains while burning the sky. Perhaps I should''ve backed off a bit or dodged them back to a middle tone. I suppose it put many people off. I also was tempted to boost the contrast on this image but most of the Ansel photos I studied were similar to this, having a majority of middle tones, a few highlights, and most of the gradation of tones in the sky or clouds. I spent about 4 or 5 hours dodging and burning, making sure I kept detail in almost all of the shadowed areas. I made an 8x12 print of this image and it looks amazing! 100x''s better than this websized version. It also appears to have more tonal range and contrast compared to the monitor as well.', '2005-03-14 05:08:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1225970, 153329, 23456, '<td valign="top">nice one,  well done !</td>', 'nice one,  well done !', '2005-03-14 05:35:30.000000', NULL, 0),
